{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact 6e63dd015d368b6e2c3e0d3e9c3a2c9936513c45. Reviewed all 29 changed paths in a separate detached checkout; reproduced npm ci, npm run check (0), npm test (52/52), npm run spike:feasibility (passed, 51 fixtures identical in Node and Chromium; the rerun changed only timings and the WASM byte count) and confirmed test:protocol, test:pds, test:runtime, test:dynamic-apps, test:flows, spike:acceptance and spike:report exit 1 as unimplemented. Independent adversarial pass plus my own probes; every finding below was reproduced at this head.\n\nBlocking:\n1. The exact head cannot land. notes/README.md conflicts with current main 7dc50bb2 (the plan-review row landed after this request was filed; git merge-tree 7dc50bb2 6e63dd01 reports the conflict). Recut on main; the recut is a new head and returns to publication and review.\n2. Determinism across host and browser: src/definition/schemas.ts admits minGraphemes/maxGraphemes, and @atproto/lexicon counts graphemes with the host's native Intl.Segmenter when present (lex-data utf8-grapheme-len.js), so a state near a grapheme bound can validate under one ICU/Unicode version and fail under another, which is a pause on one replica and effective on the other. Remove grapheme constraints from the S0 profile subset (or pin the ponyfill) and add a corpus fixture.\n3. Work is not bounded by the deterministic budgets. values.ts charges one inspection visit per value regardless of size while the exit hook re-encodes every intermediate result; measured: ($a := s \u0026 s \u0026 s; $count(state.rows.$a)) with s=200 KB, 4096 rows runs 2.66 s before value_bytes fires; the independent pass measured 11.85 s for 4000 rows with an 800 KB local at 16,017/100,000 steps and 20,020/2,000,000 nodes. The budgets admit roughly a minute of CPU per act; the browser's 15 s watchdog therefore decides outcomes by machine speed, and the Node path has no watchdog. Charge encoded bytes to a cumulative inspection budget (or memoize by identity) so the profile's bound is the bound, and say so in docs/runtime-profile.md.\n4. Engine-limit exhaustion is indistinguishable from ordinary engine errors: with stack: 64 the engine's D1011 fires before the host entry hook, so the evaluation_depth branch in evaluator.ts is dead, and a 65-term 1+1+... or $append over 8193+8193 items returns engine_error with the same code as a type error. Translate D1011/D2014 to explicit limit codes, delete the dead branch, and test both.\n5. src/definition/schemas.ts: a def with type \"constructor\" or \"__proto__\" throws TypeError (allowed.includes is not a function) instead of unsupported_schema with a path. Use Object.hasOwn on the supported table.\n6. Guards with no pinning test (removing them leaves npm test green): the inspection budget (the exhaustion fixture accepts either code and only step_budget fires), the fold-level state cap (only canonicalJson is tested directly), the stack/sequence engine options, range and regex refusal codes, the reason regex and message type, -0, key well-formedness, closed:false and duplicate-id refusal, the view byte/file/node/depth limits, and astNodes. The plan's \"test exact boundaries\" applies to these constants too.\n7. Plan section 8 asks for representative desktop and mobile screenshots preserved as review evidence; .gitignore excludes experiments/generated where they are written, so none are in the head. Commit two or record the deviation in the note.\n\nNon-blocking: version and license strings in scripts/feasibility.ts are literals (they match the lock, and report.dependencies is measured); the \"Inlay cannot access signing scope\" fixture proves a missing prop becomes an unknown component, while the real boundary is main.ts passing only {summary}; an absent result reports wire_value \"unsupported value\", which is correct but misleading; sequence 16384 is a functional cap below what 128 KiB of state can hold, not \"supplementary\"; \"AST depth 64\" is about 32 syntactic levels; $uppercase/$lowercase depend on the host's Unicode case tables, so the profile should either pin Unicode behaviour or note it.\n\nArchitecture: affects the runtime layer (architecture section 7: one pinned engine, bounded profile, deterministic limits), the definition layer (section 3: Lexicon-only IDL, runtime validation) and the interaction layer (section 9: inert declarative views). The head preserves those contracts and adds a candidate profile; the adopted notes change status lines only, which section 10 permits. Finding 2 is a contract gap inside the runtime layer, not a change of it.\n\nSecurity: confinement verified (allowlisted node types, operators and functions; lambda, apply, transform, regex, sort, wildcard, descendant, parent and range refused; $now/$millis/$random/$eval refused; hooks Symbol-keyed and unreachable; lookup is own-property only; prototype keys refused; no Date or Math.random in src). Fidelity verified (safe integers, -0, surrogates, depth 32, absent vs null and array order, byte caps at exact boundaries). Rendering verified inert (createTextNode/textContent only, no innerHTML/eval/Function/import()/fetch, XRPC resolver throws, external bodies and imports refused, zero external requests and zero render-time submissions measured). Evidence verified: committed feasibility.json source hashes match all HEAD blobs, measuredAt precedes the commit, the note's figures match the blob, go.mod has no replace, go.sum matches the recorded module checksum, no secrets, no authored DDL in atseq definitions. Unresolved: findings 2, 3 and 4 are determinism and failure-classification defects on the trust boundary between replicas; not approvable until fixed.\n\nSimplification: delete the dead depth hook; one byte-charged budget can replace inspectedNodes; checkAst walks the AST twice (collect then walk) and can be one pass. None weakens a condition.\n\nOn the recut: republish all path artifacts at the new head, name the results-note artifact first, and request fresh review. Do not adopt the plan-review recommendations implicitly; nothing here depends on them.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:e105464f7f56528ae9e419c7c1b7926d5be1b0cf","head":"6e63dd015d368b6e2c3e0d3e9c3a2c9936513c45","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:bee0bed7a08186724e2d150db579f62ad8ece2bb\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:2e2a2676e738c957f1a643dd5f9b2c20201dc0e8","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}